  "summary": "The page presents data on the expression levels of various markers on CD8+ T cells under different peptide conditions. CD160, CD244, PD-1, Lag3, Tim3, and TIGIT show varying levels of expression when no peptide, a single peptide, or repeat peptides are present. Notably, PD-1 expression reaches 99% with repeat peptide exposure, indicating significant upregulation. These findings suggest differential immune checkpoint expression based on peptide exposure."
